    "recommendations": "• Mark the driveway entrance with reflective address numbers visible from the road in both directions.\n• Trim vegetation along the access drive to maintain clear sightlines and prevent branches from blocking emergency vehicles.\n• Keep a minimum of one vehicle-width of clearance on the access drive at all times.\n• Clear vegetation between the main residence and the detached structure to allow responders to move between the two buildings without obstruction.\n• Mark or label the rear access point so responders arriving from the front can quickly locate it.\n• Keep the rear access point unlocked or fitted with a knox-box style lockbox to allow responders through without delay.\n• Trim dense vegetation near the rear of the property to allow responders to move and stage equipment safely.\n• Keep the walkway clear of stored items, equipment, or overgrown plantings that would slow responder movement.\n• Post the property address visibly at the road and again at the main entrance to the residence."
