    "recommendations": "• Thin the tree cluster nearest to the structure to create more open space between the trees and the building.\n• Trim low-hanging branches on scattered trees close to the structure so flames cannot climb from the ground into the tree canopy.\n• Cut grass around the structure short and keep it mowed regularly, especially during dry periods.\n• Remove or trim shrubs that are growing directly against or within a few feet of the structure.\n• Separate any shrubs growing beneath or between trees near the structure so fire cannot move easily from shrubs up into the trees.\n• Trim overhanging branches along the driveway so vehicles, including emergency equipment, can pass through without obstruction.\n• Keep vegetation along the driveway edges cut back to maintain clear sightlines and room for vehicles to move and turn around.\n• Remove any dead or dry plant material from around the base of the structure and near scattered shrubs.\n• Keep the open green space areas mowed and free of accumulated dry grass or debris."
